const completeChapters=[["Medical Billing کیا ہے؟", "Medical billing records healthcare services and submits claims to insurers to receive payment.", "Medical billing provider ki services ka record banakar insurance ko claim bhejne aur payment receive karne ka process hai.", "Registration → insurance check → visit/documentation → coding → bill/claim → payer processing → payment → patient balance.", "Provider ki service ka bill sahi bana kar payer ya patient se due payment lena.", "Sample patient visit workflow ترتیب سے لکھیں۔"], ["Revenue Cycle Management (RCM)", "RCM manages the financial process from scheduling through final account resolution.", "RCM appointment se le kar tamam payments, adjustments aur patient balance resolve hone tak ka financial system hai.", "Front-end: scheduling, registration, verification, authorization. Middle-end: documentation, coding, charge entry, claim. Back-end: posting, denials, AR, appeals, collections, reports.", "Front / Middle / Back End ke functions.", "Har stage ke 2 tasks list karein."], ["Patient Registration", "Collect accurate demographics and insurance information before services.", "Patient ki basic aur insurance details sahi collect karna registration hai.", "Name, DOB, address, phone, payer, Member ID, Group, policy holder, relationship, primary/secondary insurance. Errors may cause rejection.", "Registration data accuracy.", "Fictional patient registration record banayein."], ["Insurance Verification", "Verify active coverage, plan, network, PCP, referral, authorization and cost share.", "Insurance active hai ya nahi aur service ke rules/cost check karna verification hai.", "Check active status, plan/network, PCP, referral, prior auth, copay, deductible remaining, coinsurance and covered service. Eligibility = active? Benefits = coverage/cost?", "Active plan does not mean every service is automatically covered.", "Verification checklist complete karein."], ["Insurance Types", "Understand Medicare, Medicaid, commercial plans and TRICARE.", "Medicare federal program; Medicaid federal-state program; commercial private coverage; TRICARE eligible military community coverage.", "Medicare A hospital, B medical/outpatient, C Medicare Advantage, D drugs. Medicaid rules vary by state. Commercial examples UHC/Aetna/Cigna/BCBS/Humana. TRICARE eligibility rules apply.", "Coverage and rules vary by plan and patient eligibility.", "Har type ka one-line summary likhein."], ["PPO, HMO, EPO & POS", "Compare network flexibility and referral rules.", "Plans ke network, PCP aur referral rules mukhtalif hote hain.", "PPO generally more flexibility/out-of-network options; HMO typically network/PCP/referral rules; EPO usually in-network except emergency; POS combines features.", "Always verify actual plan benefits.", "PPO aur HMO ka comparison karein."], ["Patient Cost Share", "Understand copay, deductible, coinsurance and out-of-pocket maximum.", "Patient ke insurance plan ke mutabiq apne kharch ke mukhtalif types samjhein.", "Copay fixed amount; deductible plan-year amount before applicable coverage; coinsurance percentage of allowed amount; OOP max cap for covered costs subject to plan rules. Premiums/noncovered items may not count.", "Example: allowed $200, coinsurance 20% after deductible = patient $40, payer $160.", "$100 allowed amount par 10% coinsurance calculate karein."], ["Medical Coding", "Translate diagnosis and services into standard codes.", "Diagnosis aur performed services ko standardized codes dena coding hai.", "ICD-10-CM diagnosis; CPT professional services/procedures; HCPCS supplies/equipment/services; modifiers add context. Use current guidelines and documentation.", "Codes must match provider documentation and applicable rules.", "Diagnosis vs procedure code ka farq batayein."], ["Charge Entry", "Enter documented billable services into billing software.", "Documentation ke mutabiq services aur charges system mein enter karna.", "Patient, DOS, provider, diagnosis, CPT/HCPCS, modifier, units, charge, POS. Validate against documentation.", "Never guess codes or charges.", "Sample charge-entry fields fill karein."], ["Claim", "A claim requests payer payment for healthcare services.", "Claim insurance ko payment ki request hoti hai.", "Patient/payer/provider details, NPI, TIN, diagnoses, procedures, DOS, charges, POS, modifiers and units.", "Accurate claim data supports processing.", "Claim fields ka checklist banayein."], ["CMS-1500 & UB-04", "CMS-1500 is commonly for professional claims; UB-04 for institutional claims.", "Professional provider claims ke liye CMS-1500 aur institutional/facility claims ke liye UB-04 aam forms hain.", "Physicians, therapists and professionals commonly CMS-1500; hospitals/facilities generally UB-04; confirm payer requirements.", "Use the form required by payer and claim type.", "Professional vs facility claim examples."], ["EDI & Clearinghouse", "Electronic transactions transfer claim and insurance information.", "EDI electronic data exchange; clearinghouse claim data ko check/route karne mein madad karta hai.", "837 claim; 835 ERA; 270 eligibility inquiry; 271 response; 276 status inquiry; 277 response; 278 authorization/referral; 999 acknowledgment; 277CA claim acknowledgment.", "Provider/software → clearinghouse → payer; errors may return for correction.", "Transaction codes match karein."], ["Rejection vs Denial", "A rejection fails initial validation; a denial follows payer adjudication and refuses payment partly or fully.", "Rejection initial check par error se return; denial payer process ke baad payment refuse/adjust karta hai.", "Rejection examples invalid ID/NPI/DOB/format. Fix and resubmit. Denial examples auth, coverage, timely filing, medical necessity; analyze and corrected claim/appeal as appropriate.", "Follow payer instructions and deadlines.", "Ek rejection aur ek denial ka solution likhein."], ["Payment Posting", "Record payer and patient payments, adjustments and balances accurately.", "Insurance/patient payments aur adjustments claim mein post karna posting hai.", "Review EFT/ERA/EOB, claim, payment, adjustment, responsibility; post, reconcile and verify remaining balance. Example charge $200, allowed $150, paid $120, patient $30, adjustment $50.", "Reconcile payment to remittance and bank.", "Sample posting calculation karein."], ["EFT, ERA & EOB", "EFT transfers funds; ERA provides electronic remittance details; EOB explains claim processing.", "EFT paisay transfer, ERA payment ki electronic detail, EOB claim process ki explanation.", "EFT banking transaction; ERA electronic data; EOB statement/explanation. Reconcile the payment and remittance.", "They are related but not interchangeable.", "In teeno ka difference explain karein."], ["Denial Management", "Identify, investigate, correct and appeal denied claims to resolve payment.", "Denied claims ki wajah samajh kar correction, appeal ya follow-up karna.", "Receive denial, read codes, investigate, check eligibility/coding/documentation, choose corrected claim/appeal, submit, follow up and record resolution. Common reasons: eligibility, authorization, duplicate, coding, medical necessity, timely filing, COB, provider enrollment and missing information.", "Track reason, action, deadlines and outcome.", "Denial workflow sequence likhein."], ["CARC & RARC", "Adjustment reason and remark codes explain remittance adjustments.", "CARC adjustment ki reason; RARC extra remark/clarification batata hai.", "Use current official code lists and remittance context to interpret.", "Code descriptions and payer context matter.", "CARC aur RARC ka difference."], ["Corrected Claims", "Correct a previously submitted claim following payer-specific rules.", "Pehle submit claim ko payer ke rules ke mutabiq correction ke sath resubmit karna.", "Find original claim, identify correction, verify documents, apply corrected indicator/payer rule, submit and follow up.", "Do not send a corrected claim if payer requires another process.", "Corrected claim steps arrange karein."], ["Appeals", "Request payer reconsideration of a claim decision with supporting evidence.", "Payer ke decision ka dobara review mangna appeal hai.", "Include patient/member, claim, DOS, denial, rationale, evidence, records/policy, provider and contact. Workflow: review → evidence → letter → submission → follow-up → decision.", "Observe appeal deadline and payer process.", "Appeal letter ke key items list karein."], ["Accounts Receivable (AR)", "AR is money owed to provider; follow-up pursues unpaid claims.", "Provider ko jo payment milni baqi ho woh AR hai.", "Age buckets 0–30, 31–60, 61–90, 91–120, 120+. Prioritize high-dollar, deadlines, old, denied/rejected, expected payments and underpayments.", "Prioritize per client workflow and deadline risk.", "AR aging buckets explain karein."], ["Insurance Follow-up Calling", "Call payer to obtain claim status, denial reason, payment and next steps.", "Insurance ko call karke claim ka status aur action poochna.", "Prepare patient/DOB/member ID, provider/NPI/TIN, claim/DOS/amount. Ask received/processed/paid/denied, reason, documents, appeal deadline, payment date; capture reference.", "Document call reference and next action.", "Practice the provided status-call script."], ["AR Follow-up Notes", "Record concise call outcomes and next actions in billing system.", "Har follow-up ke baad clear notes record karna zaroori hai.", "Date, payer, claim status, payment, responsibility, adjustment, reference, next action and follow-up date.", "Notes prevent duplicate work and preserve history.", "Sample claim note create karein."], ["Timely Filing", "Submit claims within payer-specific deadline.", "Claim payer ki deadline ke andar submit karna timely filing hai.", "Deadline varies by payer, plan, contract and rules. Track DOS, deadline and submission proof.", "Verify payer policy; don't assume one universal limit.", "Deadline tracker fields banayein."], ["Coordination of Benefits (COB)", "Determine primary and secondary payer order when multiple coverages exist.", "Multiple insurances hon to primary/secondary order set karna COB hai.", "Primary processes first; then send secondary with primary adjudication details per secondary rules.", "Incorrect order can delay or deny payment.", "Primary vs secondary workflow describe karein."], ["Medical Necessity", "Documentation should support the service as medically appropriate under applicable policies.", "Medical record service ki medical zaroorat ko support kare.", "Physician documentation, diagnosis, clinical notes, treatment plan, records, tests and payer policy.", "Coverage policy and documentation must be checked.", "Medical necessity support documents list karein."], ["Underpayment", "Compare actual payment with expected contract/allowed reimbursement and investigate difference.", "Expected amount se kam payment ko identify aur investigate karna.", "Check fee schedule, adjustment, modifier, units, contract, processing, multiple-procedure adjustment and benefit limit; contact payer, correct/appeal and follow up.", "Use contract and payer adjudication details.", "Expected vs paid ka variance calculate karein."], ["Provider Credentialing", "Verify provider qualifications and professional credentials.", "Provider ki qualifications, license aur professional details verify karna credentialing hai.", "Education, license, board certification, work history, malpractice, DEA when applicable, NPI, taxonomy, location, references. CAQH profile, PECOS Medicare enrollment, state-specific Medicaid enrollment and commercial payer enrollment are part of the setup workflow.", "Credentialing differs from payer enrollment.", "Credentialing documents checklist."], ["NPI & Taxonomy", "NPI uniquely identifies providers; taxonomy classifies provider specialty/type.", "NPI provider ki unique ID; taxonomy provider ki specialty/classification.", "Type 1 individual (physician/NP/PA/therapist); Type 2 organization (clinic/group/hospital). Taxonomy examples family medicine, psychiatry, dermatology, cardiology.", "Verify NPI and taxonomy on submitted claims.", "Type 1/Type 2 examples."], ["EFT & ERA Enrollment", "Set up electronic payment and remittance with payers.", "Payer ke sath bank transfer aur remittance enrollment karna.", "May require provider, NPI, TIN, bank/routing, address, contact and authorized person. Protect bank details.", "Use secure handling for financial information.", "Enrollment data checklist."], ["End-to-End Workflow", "Follow the full revenue cycle from scheduling to final account resolution.", "RCM ke tamam steps ko start se finish tak samjhein.", "Scheduling → registration → verification → auth/referral → visit/documentation → coding → charge → claim scrub/submit → clearinghouse → adjudication → posting → denials/AR → appeals/corrected → patient billing → resolution.", "Workflow handoffs and status tracking matter.", "Workflow ko order mein arrange karein."], ["RCM KPIs", "Measure billing performance with clean claims, denials, AR days and collections.", "KPIs billing performance measure karte hain.", "Clean claim rate = clean/total ×100; denial rate = denied/total ×100; days in AR; net collection rate; first-pass resolution; posting accuracy; appeal success; auth denial; timely filing.", "Interpret KPIs together and define numerator/denominator consistently.", "100 mein 90 clean claims ka rate calculate karein."], ["RCM Audit", "Review registration, verification, coding, claims and payment for errors.", "Billing process audit karke errors aur compliance/revenue gaps dhoondhna.", "Audit demographics, member ID, plan, eligibility, benefits, authorization, diagnosis/CPT/modifier/units, NPI/TIN, duplicate, filing, payment, adjustment and patient responsibility.", "Audit findings should have corrective actions.", "Audit checklist banayein."], ["Revenue Leakage", "Revenue is lost when billing steps fail or collectible amounts are missed.", "Process errors ki wajah se earned revenue receive na hona leakage hai.", "Unsubmitted/late claims, coding errors, unworked denials, missed underpayments, missing auth, posting errors, patient balances, credentialing. Prevent with monitoring, queues, aging, reconciliation, audits.", "Identify causes and prevention controls.", "Leakage ka example aur prevention."], ["Billing Software & Portals", "Know common practice management systems, clearinghouses and payer portals.", "Billing software aur payer portals ke roles samjhein.", "Systems include AdvancedMD, Tebra/Kareo, athenahealth, NextGen, eClinicalWorks, DrChrono, Practice Fusion; clearinghouses Office Ally, Availity, Waystar, Claim.MD; payer portals vary.", "Access depends on client and organization.", "Software, clearinghouse, portal ka difference."], ["Client Communication", "Give clients clear updates on claims, denials, AR, payments and missing items.", "Client ko professional, concise progress update dena.", "Report performance, claim status, denial/AR, payment, credentialing, missing documents and revenue improvement. Example: pending claims are being followed up to reduce delays.", "Communicate facts, next steps and timelines.", "Client update message draft karein."], ["Medical Billing Abbreviations", "Learn frequent billing acronyms and their meanings.", "Medical billing ke common short forms yaad karein.", "RCM, NPI, TIN, CPT, ICD, HCPCS, EOB, ERA, EFT, EDI, AR, DOS, COB, PCP, PA, POS, PR, OA, CO, PI, CARC, RARC, CMS, PECOS, CAQH, HIPAA, MBI, SLA, KPI, FPL, HMO, PPO, EPO, DME, SNF, TFL, FFS, VOB, AOB.", "Understand context; one acronym can have payer-specific use.", "10 abbreviations full forms likhein."], ["Learning Roadmap", "Progress from foundation through advanced RCM.", "Foundation se advanced RCM tak stepwise learning.", "Level 1 foundation; 2 insurance; 3 verification; 4 coding; 5 claims; 6 payments; 7 denials; 8 AR; 9 credentialing; 10 advanced RCM.", "Build knowledge before complex cases.", "Apni learning level identify karein."], ["Practical Training", "Practice realistic exercises rather than memorizing definitions only.", "Practical tasks se hands-on skill develop hoti hai.", "Practice registration, insurance card data, verification, cost-share calculation, sample claim, rejection, posting, denial, corrected claim, appeal, AR call, notes, reports and credentialing checklist.", "Use fictional/sample data only.", "Choose a practical exercise and complete it."]];
